---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../config";
---

<Layout
  title="About TripAxle & How We Research"
  description="TripAxle is an independent guide to renting and driving a car in Portugal. Here is who it is for, what it is not, and how the guidance is put together."
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "About & how we research" }]} />

  <article class="prose" style="max-width: 46rem;">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>About TripAxle</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      An independent guide to renting and driving a car in Portugal, written for
      English-speaking travelers.
    </p>

    <h2>What TripAxle is</h2>
    <p>{site.trust.whyTrust}</p>
    <p>
      Every guide is built around one practical question a traveler actually
      asks — “how does pickup work at Faro?”, “what does the excess mean?”,
      “can I pay a toll after I have flown home?” — and answers it in plain
      language, with the specific things to check on your own booking.
    </p>

    <h2>What TripAxle is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It is not a rental company or a booking site.</li>
      <li>It does not rank or score rental companies.</li>
      <li>It does not publish paid or incentivised reviews.</li>
      <li>It does not run a price-comparison engine.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Where a link to a rental comparison service would genuinely help you act
      on a decision, we may add one and label it clearly. That is the only
      commercial element, and it never changes what a guide says.
    </p>

    <h2>How we research these guides</h2>
    <p>{site.trust.howWeResearch}</p>
    <p>
      Airports rearrange desks, providers change shuttle points, and fees move.
      Treat every specific detail here as “very likely, verify on your voucher,”
      not “guaranteed.” When something is commonly misunderstood, we say so
      rather than glossing over it.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If something here is out of date or does not match what you found on the
      ground, that feedback is genuinely useful and helps the next traveler.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
